  "worked_solution": "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}\\cdot {5}^{7x} & \\ge {5}^{7x-3} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\cdot {5}^{7x}-{5}^{7x-3} & \\ge 0 \\\\ ({x}^{3}-{5}^{-3})\\cdot {5}^{7x} & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${5}^{7x}$ and get\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}-{5}^{-3}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & \\ge {5}^{-3} \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}} & \\ge \\sqrt[3]{{5}^{-3}} \\\\ x & \\ge {({5}^{-3})}^{1/3} \\\\ x & \\ge {5}^{-1} \\\\ x & \\ge \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $x\\ge \\frac{1}{5}.$",
